      "content": "That feeling of being obsolete, like your entire foundation has crumbled, is a deep and heavy kind of despair. When the things that gave your life meaning suddenly become irrelevant, it can feel like there's nothing left to hold onto. It's okay to feel that the chapter you knew is over, but that doesn't mean the story has to end; sometimes, a quiet, necessary pause is all it takes to find a new direction.",
      "source": "target",
